1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his trial, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
I'll win, even if he is a captain. I'll win!

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The test to see who would fight the Eye of the Midnight Sun was winding down.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
There! See? You're getting it now!

7
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The end result was a victory for Yuno, Noelle, and En of Team P.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Then, the identity of the mysterious mage who called himself Xerx was unveiled.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
We need your trap magic and your ability to think critically.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The exam is done, and you likely passed. I hope you'll join.

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Isn't it time that you wore your robe? The robe of your true squad, Zora Ideale.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Don't know who you're talking about.

13
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Me? I'm just some lame excuse for a super mage who happened to be passing through.

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
so

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,000
.

16
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,200
up

17
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:12,220
Hey look, Asta isn't budging an inch. He's just like a statue.

18
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:14,140
Is he still breathing?

19
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:20,360
Yeah, as far as I can tell. But he isn't himself. Losing the tournament must have hit him really hard.

20
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,520
He seemed awfully busted up over it.

21
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:27,840
I will catch up to you! I will be the Wizard King! I swear!

22
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:35,060
I can't blame the poor guy. Not only did his childhood buddy win the whole thing, but I don't think Asta was expecting him to have that much power.

23
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:40,340
And the shock of being surpassed by his long-standing rival may keep getting worse with every day that passes.

24
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:45,520
Trust me, I understand the feeling. My sister. My goddess. Marie.

25
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:51,620
Each day I have to endure without seeing your beautiful smile that damaged my body and soul grows ever deeper.

26
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:54,920
Forgive me for being so blunt, but I don't think that's the same thing at all.

27
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:59,120
Hey, I know. Maybe I need to launch a little surprise attack on him.

28
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,920
Nothing cheers a person up like a fun life-or-death battle.

29
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:04,320
Lightning magic! Thunderbolt destructed!

30
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:07,660
Don't you dare! Fighting is not going to help Asta right now.

31
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,560
We won't know for sure unless we try!

32
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:11,240
I think it's safe to assume.

33
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,500
He'll kill him!

34
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:16,060
Well, if I can't use magic, then can I at least pummel him with a brick?

35
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,200
So not happening.

36
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:31,720
Come on, Asta. Why are you still sitting here staring into space, huh?

37
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:35,320
This is because you couldn't go up against that lady killer you know.

38
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,220
It's okay, right, Rouge?

39
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:42,360
Even if it didn't go quite like you wanted, you did great out there, kiddo.

40
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:44,700
I'm sure you passed with flying colors.

41
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:48,160
So give me a big smile, okay, honey?

42
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:51,580
You better smile or I'm going to make you smile.

43
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,120
What the heck is she trying to do?

44
00:04:58,220 --> 00:04:59,300
That's so nice.

45
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:03,200
She's acting excessively cheerful in an attempt to bring Asta out of his funk.

46
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:03,760
Huh?

47
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:06,420
Yeah, I'm familiar with the tactic.

48
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:10,980
I act that way on the outside to conceal my sadness when I can't be around Marie.

49
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,620
Well, what are we waiting for, everyone?

50
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,520
We need to follow her lead and be positive.

51
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:17,220
You're right. That idiot needs a confidence boost.

52
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,660
Oh, nice. So does that mean I can start attacking him now?

53
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:20,540
What is wrong with you?

54
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:25,400
What did I just say, luck?

55
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,720
Are you still alive, Asta?

56
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:32,020
Hey, wait. Isn't it about that time?

57
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:35,440
To see the Royal Knight Selection Exam results.

58
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:38,580
They're supposed to be coming here by outpost really soon.

59
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:41,320
Oh, that's right. Guess it must have slipped my mind.

60
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:44,100
That outpost should show up any minute now, Asta.

61
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:49,160
Look, once you make the cut, you're going to catch back up to Mr. Cool in no time.

62
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:51,100
Then you can leave him in the dust.

63
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,120
I'm not so sure.

64
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,280
Will I even get in?

65
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,460
I mean, I did get eliminated, remember?

66
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,680
Don't sweat the small stuff, sweetie.

67
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:02,820
She's right. You need to have some more faith in yourself.

68
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,000
But Noelle...

69
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:08,320
Of course I did win in the finals, so obviously I'm going to be selected for the Royal Knights.

70
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:09,940
Results like that speak for themselves.

71
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:13,700
You only won because you were lucky enough to be on the same team as Pretty Boy.

72
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:15,100
That's still better than you.

73
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:17,400
Your magic was what caused your team to lose.

74
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:20,240
I can't believe you would dare to address your superior like that.

75
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,720
Don't talk to me like I'm some clueless rookie.

76
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,360
I am royalty, you know.

77
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,740
And nobody cares, you know.

78
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,620
I feel like that's so old.

79
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:27,980
Could you just please stop my doing?

80
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,700
Fine. Whatever.

81
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:34,280
Just stop worrying about Asta and concentrate on your own chances.

82
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,960
Huh? But there's nothing for me to be worried about.

83
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:40,780
I totally made it into the Royal Knights, so I ain't sweating it one bit.

84
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:41,920
You know what I'm saying?

85
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:44,740
Well, Narnie, you're completely terrified, aren't you?

86
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,920
No way. Don't be stupid.

87
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,080
And cool.

88
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:57,660
All right, fine. I suppose I could make an exception this once.

89
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:01,980
To lift your spirits, I'll let you look at Marie's photograph for three and a half seconds.

90
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:04,600
I've got a way better idea. Spore with me, Asta.

91
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:05,540
Huh?

92
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,940
I bet you're already feeling better.

93
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,880
Stop it. There's no way he's better.

94
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,960
Let me hit him with one full throttle attack.

95
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,440
I told you, you can't.

96
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,920
Oh, no. Charmy.

97
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:18,040
Hmm? What's gotten into you, girl?

98
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:23,080
I can't stop thinking about how cool Yuna was during that battle.

99
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:27,220
It's making my chest high in so much that I can barely swallow any food.

100
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:29,860
I've only eaten a fifth of it.

101
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,280
Yeah, you're fine.

102
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,740
You're not gonna say anything?

103
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,900
Oh, man. This is serious.

104
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:39,400
My incredible savior of sustenance.

105
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,220
My heart won't stop begging for you.

106
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,680
I'm pretty sure that's heartburn.

107
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:44,960
It looks like she's in bad shape, too.

108
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:45,940
I'll say.

109
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,260
But what can we do?

110
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:48,260
Hey!

111
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,060
How about a nice bath?

112
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:50,680
Hmm?

113
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:50,940
Huh?

114
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:51,740
Ah!

115
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:55,980
What up, boss?

116
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,680
What's this about about?

117
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:01,540
You're bound to cheer up after sweating it out in some piping hot water.

118
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,080
Come on. Let's go.

119
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,940
Thanks, but I don't really feel up to it.

120
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:10,320
Your captain orders you to, so quit your bellyaching and get in.

121
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:18,800
What'd I tell you?

122
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,540
A nice bath like this is just what the doctor ordered.

123
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:22,720
I guess so.

124
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:28,580
You're gonna get boiled alive if you do that one more time, you understand me.

125
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:37,120
How are you ladies doing? You warm enough?

126
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:40,620
It's perfect, Captain Yami. Thanks for asking.

127
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:44,180
I can't believe we're all sharing a bath. So embarrassing.

128
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:51,480
Oh, come on.

129
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:55,300
Damn, those chatty ladies sure are making a lot of racket.

130
00:08:55,300 --> 00:09:01,020
Anyway, your situation really gets me thinking.

131
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,660
Huh? About what?

132
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,480
Shut your yap and I'll tell you.

133
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:10,960
It reminds me of a time when I just joined up with the Magic Knight Squad by the name of the Gray Deer.

134
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:11,680
Huh?

135
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,880
They're called the Aqua Deer now.

136
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:18,380
But this happened back when old Julius was their captain, so the name was different then.

137
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,260
That makes sense.

138
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,720
That's good. Now be quiet and listen to the story.

139
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:25,320
I've been doing some warrior training to beat myself up a bit, right?

140
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,900
It's story time all of a sudden.

141
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:28,840
Shoot.

142
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:34,180
I got hungry, so I decided to try catching some fish.

143
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:39,720
But then, I could eat a horse right now. I'm so hungry.

144
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:43,780
Come on, I don't have all day now.

145
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,240
Bite the damn thing.

146
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,500
Gotta catch something.

147
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:48,760
Gotcha.

148
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:48,840
Gotcha.

149
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:53,980
Perfect.

150
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,540
You stole the bait.

151
00:09:55,540 --> 00:10:05,040
Fishing is a breeze out on the open sea, but all this fiddly stuff really isn't my style.

152
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:08,440
Yep, I'm gonna starve to death.

153
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,240
This is Shakedown?

154
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:26,040
If you're looking for a fight, you've found one.

155
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:33,980
But being hungry tends to make me irritable, so I wouldn't expect a lot of mercy if I were you.

156
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,340
Here you are.

157
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:43,960
Forgive the intrusion, Sir Magic Knight, but you look like you could use something to eat.

158
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,940
You didn't put poison in these or anything, did you?

159
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,840
Of course not. That would be absurd.

160
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:50,860
Go on. Have some.

161
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:52,360
Well, I am kind of starving.

162
00:10:55,300 --> 00:11:00,300
If you don't mind, we'd be happy to give you more in exchange for hearing our plea.

163
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,440
Is that something you would consider, Sir?

164
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,100
Sure, why not?

165
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:17,680
You see, harvest time will soon be at hand, and we're fortunate to be expecting a bountiful crop this year.

166
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,740
Okay, good for you, I guess.

167
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,340
Not exactly.

168
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:21,640
Huh?

169
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:26,080
They're coming to take it away. We're not sure what to do.

170
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,520
Who's they?

171
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,020
Bandits, of course.

172
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:33,740
They wait until we gather the crops we so diligently grew and harvested.

173
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:38,000
Then they come along and steal everything from us before we even realize what's happening.

174
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:46,240
We've tried submitting an appeal with the royal capital, but it seems we're not the only ones having this problem, and they're a bit short-staffed.

175
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:48,280
A village like ours isn't a priority.

176
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:52,760
Okay, so you brought me here because you want me to put the herd on some bandits for you, is that it?

177
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:57,880
Not for nothing. We fully intend to provide all of your meals while you're here. Three a day!

178
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:05,380
How dare you? You've got a lot of nerve. A good magic knight deserves more than food for his services.

179
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:11,680
But we have no money. The bandits took last year's harvest as well, so we're utterly impoverished.

180
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,940
Even that bread we gave you comes from our secret supply.

181
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:21,140
I want naps, too. Meals alone won't cut it. I need my shut-eye, and that's final.

182
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:27,160
How about that? Either you accept my conditions, or I'm not going to help save your wimpy little village.

183
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:33,400
Sounds like we've got ourselves a deal then. Well, I guess I've had about enough to eat.

184
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,640
So I think I'll go take mine now.

185
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:41,360
Wait, magic knight! I'm afraid we never had the opportunity to ask for your name.

186
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:45,440
It's Yami. Yami Sukihiro.

187
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:57,760
I'm kind of disappointed.

188
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,180
What's the matter, boss?

189
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:06,420
They've got another bumper crop this year. That really is too bad. We'll have to pull it all up by the roots.

190
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:10,620
I'm thinking it might be too heavy to carry back.

191
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:17,120
Oh, that's no problem. We got a guy who can use spatial magic. We'll bundle it and send it to the hideout.

192
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,260
Well, well, isn't that convenient.

193
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:31,180
Let's go! I'm sure those villagers will be waiting for us. Don't hesitate to crush them. Seal everything you can, no matter who gets in your way.

194
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:31,860
Yes, sir!

195
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:43,120
Let's see. Where do I begin? Which way leads to the granary? There? Should be straight ahead of you on the right.

196
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:44,440
Thanks.

197
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:45,560
Huh?

198
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:55,040
If I chase you away, you'll probably come back later. So I guess I better do something to make sure you never try to steal from this village again.

199
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,000
All right, that's one down.

200
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,820
Two down. Piece of cake.

201
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,500
And this bozo makes it three.

202
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:17,260
Eighteen, twenty, they just keep on coming.

203
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,340
How many are there?

204
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:40,160
What a surprise.

205
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:44,720
I see. They hired some two-bit magic knight to work security.

206
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,600
I take it you're the one who's in charge of this whole outfit?

207
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:51,000
You sure managed to scrape together plenty of small fries.

208
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:54,660
Working as a team, enough small fries can overpower the mightiest whale.

209
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:58,020
Just as it only takes one tiny termite to sink a massive galleon.

210
00:14:58,400 --> 00:15:01,660
Now, men, let's teach this fool that there's strength in numbers.

211
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,960
A reward for whoever can kill him first.

212
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:04,400
Right!

213
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:10,400
Huh. They're not really a threat by themselves.

214
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,580
But there's too damn many of them.

215
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,420
What's the plan?

216
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:19,060
Well, not much else to do,

217
00:15:19,260 --> 00:15:21,340
but cut you down one by one.

218
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:26,120
Gotcha!

219
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:26,740
Gotcha!

220
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:27,740
Gotcha!

221
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,740
Okay, who the hell are you?

222
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,240
I'm not an enemy.

223
00:15:56,740 --> 00:16:05,740
Weird shoes, weird pants, weird clothes, weird cape, and that mask. It's goofy as hell.

224
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:09,740
You say you're not, but you look pretty shady in that peacock costume of yours.

225
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:19,740
Yami, I believe your name was. Watch my back if you wouldn't mind.

226
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:22,740
Hey, wait. I remember telling you what my name was, pal.

227
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:25,740
Oh well.

228
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:41,740
This guy, he moves like he's able to read my mind or something.

229
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:46,740
Our key must be on the same wavelength.

230
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:55,740
No, what happened? How did the two of you take down so many?

231
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:56,740
Well, that's done.

232
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:57,740
Now there's just you!

233
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,740
Make a portal! Hurry!

234
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:00,740
Yes, sir!

235
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:04,740
Hey, shrimp. Why'd you stay here and let your boss get away? Huh?

236
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:19,740
The bandit's boss may have barely slipped through our fingers, but we did round up all of his underlings. They won't be attacking this or any other village for a long while.

237
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:28,740
You got that right. Now, you never did give me a clear answer. I think I'd remember if I met somebody like you, so how did you know my name?

238
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:43,740
Oh, yes, you did ask me that. The truth is, you're famous. The roughneck from a foreign land who was chosen to join the Grey Deer isn't easily forgotten about.

239
00:17:43,740 --> 00:17:45,740
Uh-huh. All right, then tell me who you are.

240
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:49,740
